{"id": "55d28d6a-d5b2-4ee3-bef9-cc6459eba40e", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "With only 8 days of data, usage sits at about 2.39 GB out of roughly 925 GB usable capacity. Looking at growth from Nov 2 to Nov 9, it's about +152MB over 7 days, averaging ~21.7MB/day, but the daily deltas seem to be decelerating rather than staying constant.

At the average growth rate, filling the remaining 922.8 GB would take roughly 42,470 days (~116 years); even at the peak observed rate of 81MB/day, it'd still be about 31 years. Even applying a more conservative 80% utilization threshold for FSx ONTAP, that still leaves tens of thousands of days of headroom, so this is clearly not a near-term concern.

"}]}
